-- Vocabulary V5 step by step (IELTS-V5 v1.1.0): five guided steps and one mixed check, in the Lesson 6 format
-- (LEARN FIRST worked example, an explanation for every answer). Auto-marked, so filed as reading tasks; every item is
-- mapped to the vocabulary subskill it practises. Owner instruction 2026-10-28 13:01 (Asia/Bishkek): 'Go next'.
-- Named-student pilot with requires_review; nothing is released. Source: docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json.
do $steps$
declare art constant text := '

- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

THE PASSAGE: A new sports centre

A. The town''s new sports centre, which opened in March after almost three years of construction, replaces a building that had become too expensive to maintain. It contains a twenty-five-metre swimming pool, two sports halls, a climbing wall and several outdoor courts. The architects were asked to minimise energy consumption, and the result is one of the most efficient public buildings in the region: solar panels on the roof generate around a third of its electricity, while rainwater collected from the roof is filtered and used in the toilets and changing rooms.

B. Accessibility was another priority. All entrances are at ground level, the pool has a moveable floor that can be raised for swimmers who need shallow water, and the changing rooms include several spaces designed for families and for people with disabilities. Local disability groups were consulted at an early stage, and several of their recommendations were adopted in the final design, including clearer signs, quieter hand dryers and a hoist to help wheelchair users into the pool.

C. Membership has exceeded expectations. Within six weeks of opening, more than two thousand residents had registered, and the management is now considering longer opening hours at weekends. The most popular facilities so far are the climbing wall and the evening yoga classes, which are frequently fully booked. To improve affordability, the council has introduced reduced prices for students, pensioners and people who are unemployed.

D. The centre has not been without criticism. Some residents complained that the car park, which has only eighty spaces, is insufficient for a building of this size, particularly on Saturday mornings when children''s swimming lessons take place. The council responded by introducing a new bus route that stops outside the main entrance and by installing secure storage for more than a hundred bicycles.

E. Running the centre requires a team of around forty staff, including lifeguards, fitness instructors and cleaners, many of whom previously worked at the old building. The management has introduced a training programme so that all staff hold a recognised first-aid qualification, and several instructors have completed additional courses in teaching swimming to adults, a service for which there has been unexpectedly strong demand. Local schools also use the pool on weekday mornings, an arrangement that provides the centre with a reliable income during hours when few adult members visit.

F. Others questioned the decision to demolish the old building rather than renovate it. The council argued that renovation would have cost almost as much as a new building while producing a centre that was far less efficient. Independent engineers who reviewed the plans broadly supported this conclusion, although they noted that the demolition itself had generated a considerable amount of waste, much of which could not be recycled.';
begin
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r82-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V5 step 1 of 6: What does the gap need?','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then decide what kind of word each gap needs.','Look at the words around the gap: after ''a/the'' a noun; after ''several/two'' a plural; after ''very'' an adjective; after a verb an adverb.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "Prices rose ______ last year.", "accepted_answers": ["E"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a noun"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a plural noun"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  a verb"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  an adjective"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  an adverb"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "There are several ______ near the station.", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a noun"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a plural noun"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  a verb"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  an adjective"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  an adverb"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "The council made a final ______ about the bridge.", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a noun"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a plural noun"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  a verb"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  an adjective"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  an adverb"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "The new system is very ______.", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a noun"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a plural noun"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  a verb"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  an adjective"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  an adverb"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "Visitors must ______ their tickets online.", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a noun"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a plural noun"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  a verb"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  an adjective"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  an adverb"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "Two ______ were closed for repairs.", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a noun"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a plural noun"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  a verb"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  an adjective"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  an adverb"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 6, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 E, an adverb: it describes how prices rose (rose significantly).\n2 B, a plural noun: ''several'' needs a plural (several facilities).\n3 A, a noun: ''a final ______'' needs a noun (a final decision).\n4 D, an adjective: after ''very'' (very effective).\n5 C, a verb: after ''must'' (must book).\n6 B, a plural noun: after ''two'' (two courts).\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Word classes: identify the word form a gap needs from the grammar around it."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: the words around the gap tell you

Before you look for the answer, decide what kind of word the gap needs.
- after a / an / the / this: a NOUN (''a ______ about the bridge'')
- after several / many / two: a PLURAL noun (''several ______'')
- after very / more / quite, or before a noun: an ADJECTIVE (''very ______'')
- after a verb, describing how: an ADVERB (''rose ______'')
- after to / must / can: a VERB (''must ______ online'')

WORKED EXAMPLE
''There has been a marked ______ in air quality.''
''a marked ______ in'' -> after ''a'' + adjective, before ''in'': a noun. -> improvement

Now decide six times.'),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'4e2551f13e2f519d4be3cf353dffd1aba3a8eefbcc2e3aaa0ed0ed3a30ae3ec1',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r83-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V5 step 2 of 6: Choose the right form','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then choose the form of the word that fits each sentence.','Decide the word class first, then choose the ending: -tion/-ment/-ity for nouns, -al/-ive/-able for adjectives, -ly for adverbs.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "The ______ of the library took two years.", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  renovating"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  renovation"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  renovate"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  renovated"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "Public transport has become more ______ since fares were cut.", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  affordably"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  affordability"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  afford"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  affordable"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "The centre is run very ______.", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  efficiently"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  efficiencies"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  efficiency"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  efficient"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "There has been a significant ______ in water quality.", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  improve"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  improved"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  improving"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  improvement"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "Many people questioned the ______ to close the pool.", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  decide"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  decided"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  decision"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  decisive"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "Cycling is popular because it is ______ friendly.", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  environmentally"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  environment"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  environments"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  environmental"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 7, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 B, renovation: after ''The'', before ''of'', you need a noun.\n2 D, affordable: after ''more'' in ''has become more ______'' you need an adjective.\n3 A, efficiently: it describes how the centre is run, so it needs an adverb.\n4 D, improvement: after ''a significant'' you need a noun.\n5 C, decision: after ''the'', you need a noun.\n6 A, environmentally: an adverb before the adjective ''friendly''.\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Derivational word formation: choose the correct member of a word family for a sentence."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: endings show the word class

One word family, many forms. The ending shows the word class:
- NOUN: -tion / -sion (renovation, decision), -ment (improvement), -ity (popularity)
- ADJECTIVE: -al (environmental), -ive (effective), -able (affordable), -ient (efficient)
- ADVERB: -ly (efficiently, significantly)

WORKED EXAMPLE
''Cycling has grown in ______ over the last decade.''
''grown in ______'' needs a noun. popular -> popularity.

Now choose six forms.'),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'871fdae6fef75d5100dd18bb885993b28d0fc2eaf4f77b529395e021118fe4f9',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r84-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V5 step 3 of 6: Copy the exact form','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then complete each sentence with ONE WORD from the passage. Copy its exact form.','The sentence is a paraphrase; the passage word may be in a different form nearby. Copy the form the gap needs, exactly.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "The centre replaced a building that had become too expensive to ________.", "accepted_answers": ["maintain"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "Solar panels on the roof ________ around a third of the centre''s electricity.", "accepted_answers": ["generate"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "All ________ to the centre are at ground level.", "accepted_answers": ["entrances"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "Within six weeks, more than two thousand residents had ________.", "accepted_answers": ["registered"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "All staff must hold a recognised first-aid ________.", "accepted_answers": ["qualification"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "Much of the waste from the demolition could not be ________.", "accepted_answers": ["recycled"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "answer_format": "text"}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 8, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 maintain (paragraph A): \"a building that had become too expensive to maintain\". After ''to'' you need a verb.\n2 generate (paragraph A): \"solar panels on the roof generate around a third of its electricity\".\n3 entrances (paragraph B): \"All entrances are at ground level\". Copy the plural.\n4 registered (paragraph C): \"more than two thousand residents had registered\". Copy the -ed form.\n5 qualification (paragraph E): \"all staff hold a recognised first-aid qualification\".\n6 recycled (paragraph F): \"much of which could not be recycled\". After ''be'' you need the -ed form.\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Locate specific detail: find the exact word form in a passage when the question is paraphrased."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: same meaning, exact form

Completion questions paraphrase the passage, so the right word may sit next to words you do not expect.
1. Decide what kind of word the gap needs.
2. Find the sentence with the same meaning.
3. Copy the word EXACTLY: spelling, plural and form all count.

WORKED EXAMPLE
''Design goal: keep the building''s energy ______ as low as possible.''
Needs a noun after ''energy''. Passage: "The architects were asked to minimise energy consumption".
Copy: consumption.

Now complete six sentences.' || art),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'aa61eee953c71711a278a77438fb6e3ee2b955dadaf75ba4db5110f209ae7353',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r85-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V5 step 4 of 6: Spelling traps','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then choose the correct spelling. Three options in each question are misspelt.','Learn the trap in each word: double letters (committee, accessible), -ate- (separate), -ely (definitely).','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "not joined together; apart", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "fe66c90a-e788-44f7-8caa-4e0019026729", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  seperete"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  seperate"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  separete"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  separate"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "easy to enter or use, for example for wheelchair users", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "fe66c90a-e788-44f7-8caa-4e0019026729", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  accessible"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  acessible"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  accesible"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  accessable"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "certainly; without any doubt", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "fe66c90a-e788-44f7-8caa-4e0019026729", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  definitly"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  definately"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  definitely"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  defenitely"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "a group of people chosen to make decisions", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "fe66c90a-e788-44f7-8caa-4e0019026729", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  comittee"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  committe"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  committee"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  commitee"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "doing a job that needs special training", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "fe66c90a-e788-44f7-8caa-4e0019026729", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  profesional"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  proffesional"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  professionnal"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  professional"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "a suggestion about what should be done", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "fe66c90a-e788-44f7-8caa-4e0019026729", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  recommendation"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  recomendation"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  recommendasion"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  reccommendation"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 5, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 D, separate: s-e-p-a-r-a-t-e. Remember ''a rat'' in the middle.\n2 A, accessible: double c, double s, and -ible.\n3 C, definitely: d-e-f-i-n-i-t-e-l-y. It comes from ''finite''.\n4 C, committee: double m, double t, double e.\n5 D, professional: one f, double s, one n.\n6 A, recommendation: one c, double m, -tion.\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Control spelling: spell high-frequency IELTS words correctly."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: one wrong letter loses the mark

In completion questions a misspelt word scores zero, even if the meaning is right.
Common traps:
- double letters: accommodation (cc, mm), committee (mm, tt, ee), accessible (cc, ss)
- vowels you cannot hear: separate (-par-), definitely (-nite-)
- -ence / -ance, -able / -ible: independence, accessible

WORKED EXAMPLE
''needed'': necessary or neccessary or necessery?
One c, double s: necessary.

Now choose six correct spellings.'),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'b2818b2ed680ff42895ad55f3fc6be6c063cd8e1d041030123cc0c8d1bc8be9c',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r86-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V5 step 5 of 6: Find the error','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Each sentence has ONE error of form, number or spelling. Write the correct word.','Check each word against the grammar around it: plural after numbers, noun after ''a'', adverb after a verb, and uncountable nouns with no -s.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "''The centre has two sport hall.'' The correct word is ________.", "accepted_answers": ["halls"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c57e0932-8d1d-4bae-9cfd-d87a0ee00bf6", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "''The council made a recommend to reduce prices.'' The correct word is ________.", "accepted_answers": ["recommendation"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "''Membership grew rapid after the centre opened.'' The correct word is ________.", "accepted_answers": ["rapidly"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "''The car park is unsufficient on Saturdays.'' The correct word is ________.", "accepted_answers": ["insufficient"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c57e0932-8d1d-4bae-9cfd-d87a0ee00bf6", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "''The staff gave us some useful advices.'' The correct word is ________.", "accepted_answers": ["advice"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c57e0932-8d1d-4bae-9cfd-d87a0ee00bf6", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "''Several facility were closed during the storm.'' The correct word is ________.", "accepted_answers": ["facilities"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c57e0932-8d1d-4bae-9cfd-d87a0ee00bf6", "answer_format": "text"}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 6, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 halls: after ''two'' you need a plural.\n2 recommendation: after ''a'' you need a noun.\n3 rapidly: it describes how membership grew, so it needs an adverb.\n4 insufficient: the negative of ''sufficient'' takes in-, not un-.\n5 advice: it is uncountable, so it has no plural -s.\n6 facilities: after ''several'' you need a plural, and -y changes to -ies.\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Word classes and formation: correct errors of form, number and spelling in completed answers."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: check every answer before you move on

Most lost marks in completion come from one of these:
- FORM: a verb where a noun is needed (''made a decide'' -> decision)
- NUMBER: no plural after a number (''two bicycle'' -> bicycles)
- ADVERB: an adjective after a verb (''rose significant'' -> significantly)
- UNCOUNTABLE: no -s on advice, equipment, information, research
- NEGATIVE PREFIX: insufficient, impossible, unusual

WORKED EXAMPLE
''The museum needs new equipments.''  ''Equipment'' is uncountable. -> equipment

Now correct six sentences. Write only the corrected word.'),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'2c23ea7a41ecb472cc32d608c7c48ab243224f31fad3c0e9f425558351998c2e',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r87-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V5 step 6 of 6: Mixed check','reading','independent_check','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then answer six new questions. Work on your own, without notes, a dictionary or help. Tell your teacher if anything interrupted you.','Use the whole routine: decide the word class, find the meaning, copy or write the exact form, and check spelling and number.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "The council has promised to ______ the old swimming pool.", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  renovating"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  renovative"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  renovate"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  renovation"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "Some residents said the ________ to demolish the old building was a mistake.", "accepted_answers": ["decision"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "people who live in a place", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "fe66c90a-e788-44f7-8caa-4e0019026729", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  residentes"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  residents"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  recidents"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  residants"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "''Swimming lessons for adult are very popular.'' The correct word is ________.", "accepted_answers": ["adults"], "taxonomy_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "supporting_node_id": "c57e0932-8d1d-4bae-9cfd-d87a0ee00bf6", "answer_format": "text"}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "The changing rooms were designed ______ for families.", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "c3f8634b-03c1-4218-b582-05afc24e4eff", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  specification"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  specifically"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  specific"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  specify"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "Local schools give the centre a reliable ________ on weekday mornings.", "accepted_answers": ["income"], "taxonomy_node_id": "be5b2be3-ffb1-4cfb-95c8-cb9e3e9101de", "supporting_node_id": "dded4435-86bc-4f98-a822-5796ab2c9540", "answer_format": "text"}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 8, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 C, renovate: after ''to'' you need a verb.\n2 decision (paragraph F): \"Others questioned the decision to demolish the old building\".\n3 B, residents: r-e-s-i-d-e-n-t-s, with -ent, not -ant.\n4 adults: ''for adult'' needs a plural here (adults in general).\n5 B, specifically: an adverb describing ''designed''.\n6 income (paragraph E): \"an arrangement that provides the centre with a reliable income\".\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Word form, spelling and exact copying from a passage."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: the whole routine

1. What kind of word does the gap need?
2. Which form ends that way (-tion, -ment, -al, -ly, plural)?
3. From a passage: copy it exactly. On your own: check the spelling.
4. Check number: plural after ''several'', no -s on uncountable nouns.

WORKED EXAMPLE
''The ______ of the centre is now considering longer weekend hours.''
Needs a noun (the people who run it). Passage: "the management is now considering longer opening hours at weekends".  -> management

Now answer six new questions on your own.' || art),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'57f1af81fe4686f43222cb3acaed701dc97fc9a2dc485dec551e56f8349e5bbb',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
end $steps$;
